lantern-plan 1
# plan-on-the-map
#title Show a plan's stages and progress on the Lantern map
#opened 2026-10-26

#goal Lantern reads the plans under .lantern/plans and shows each plan's stages, open questions and item progress.
#goal A selected stage lights up the features and files it changes on the macro view.

#scope-in Read plan files and the pull requests that tick their items, in the main process.
#scope-in A stage list with its open questions and item status.
#scope-in Highlight a selected stage's impact on the macro view.
#scope-out Planning, approving or editing a plan from the app; the lantern-plan skill does that.

#impact area explore-the-map Plans are read where the map is read and drawn over it.
#impact area review-changes A plan's items are ticked by pull requests, so the PR objects feed it.
#impact feature macro-view The stage impact is drawn as a highlight on the macro view.
#impact feature pull-requests PR objects carry the plan item they tick.
#impact file src/main/lantern-prs.ts Item status comes from the PR states this file derives.
#impact file src/main/lantern.ts The map loader hands the plans to the renderer next to the map.
#impact new src/main/lantern-plans.ts Loads every plan file with the pull requests that tick its items.

#stage s1 Read plans in the main process
#item s1.1 Load every plan with the pull requests that tick its items
#touch file src/main/lantern-prs.ts
#touch file src/main/lantern.ts
#touch new src/main/lantern-plans.ts
#accept A test loads a repo with one plan and two PRs and gets one open and one merged item.
#item s1.2 Hand the plans to the renderer next to the map
#touch file src/main/main.ts
#accept The renderer receives the plan list when a project opens, and an empty list without plans.
#question s1.q1 Do plans on other branches show, or only the checked-out one?
#touch file src/main/lantern.ts
#answer jun Only the checked-out branch for now.

#stage s2 Show the plan on the map
#item s2.1 List a plan's stages with their questions and item status
#touch feature macro-view
#touch file src/renderer/lib/macroview/model.ts
#accept A stage with an unanswered question reads as blocked in the stage list.
#item s2.2 Highlight what a selected stage changes
#touch file src/renderer/lib/macroview/marks.ts
#accept Selecting stage s1 marks the files s1 touches and nothing else.
#question s2.q1 Does the stage list sit in the review pane or beside the macro view?
#touch file src/renderer/lib/macroview/mount.ts
#explain The review pane is the narrow column of the pull request review; the macro view is the large map beside it.
#explain A list in the pane scrolls away with the review, while a list beside the map stays in view as you pick a stage.
#story Reader opens a plan on the map
#step actor Reader
#step action opens
#step subject a plan
#file src/renderer/lib/macroview/mount.ts
#below interaction sees the stages beside the map
#below consequence the list sits in the review pane => the list sits beside the map

#risk Reading plans from many branches could multiply the git scans; stay on the checked-out branch.
#risk A plan edited after approval must show as changed, not as approved.

